  "notes": ["The original count policy comes from the archive-loaded normal Sasuke actor. Branch probes declare the current selector, cached movement state and input pulse rather than qualifying the complete controller or physical stick path.","Ground takeoff entry does not spend; ascent and an admitted relaunch entry add one point. A relaunch request alone does not spend. The fall leaf requires readiness; the active dash leaf does not, but both require a pulse, a clear input lock and a count below three.","The ordinary falling dash leaf admits the buffered flick at every tested count. Wind-up seeds zero to one and leaves all nonzero counts and the meter unchanged at the observed entry cut.","The landing entry clears the airborne state without resetting used points. The next grounded resource prefix clears the count. The floor collision that requests landing is not run in these specific branches.","The portable test matches seed and reset order only. Native takeoff already moves on its accepted jump update; no original pose clock, dash budget, chain, height, collision or complete actor admission is implied."],
